[Desktop Entry]
{{!-- Handlebars template for the .desktop file Tauri generates. Tauri's own
  template writes the Exec line with no argument placeholder, which is why a .fw
  file double-clicked in a file manager never reached the app: the launcher had
  nowhere to put the path. It also emits no Keywords, no StartupNotify, and an
  empty Categories line unless bundle.category is set.

  %F, not %U. The app parses argv into a PathBuf (document_path_from_arguments
  in src/lib.rs), so it needs local paths. %U would hand it a file:// URL, which
  still ends in .fw and so is accepted, and which then fails to open because no
  file by that name exists. %F is the placeholder for local paths, and it lets
  the file manager mount remote locations first.

  StartupWMClass is written out literally rather than taken from the exec
  variable, because the app sets its own GLib program name to the app id -- see
  the comment in run().

  The available variables are categories, comment, exec, icon, name, mime_type
  and long_description. There is no variable for the file name, which is always
  <productName>.desktop, so the deb and rpm neutralise this entry and ship
  com.framework.canvas.desktop instead. What this template is really for is the
  AppImage, which reuses the deb's data directory but not its custom file list
  and so has no other way to get a correct entry. --}}
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name={{name}}
GenericName=Data Canvas
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %F
Icon={{icon}}
StartupWMClass=com.framework.canvas
StartupNotify=true
Terminal=false
Categories=Office;Spreadsheet;
Keywords=spreadsheet;dataframe;data;canvas;analysis;table;csv;parquet;
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}};
{{/if}}
